"Visually, Conflict Zone is well on its way toward making a name for itself on Dreamcast. From the tanks to the helicopters all of the objects in the game are nicely textured and well represented. Take a look at the screenshots of the game in the margin to get an idea of what's in store. Along side the solid models, there's also some expected and welcomed lighting and special effects, also represented in our delicious screens, courtesy of the gang at Red Storm.<p>
Battles are sure to be blast-happy. Ranks, infantry, hummers, helicopters, stealth bombers and more. Need I continue? I didn't think so. By now, it's easy to say that Conflict Zone looks like a refreshing addition to a genre with a game library that has recently been bogged down by less-than-inspiring attempts. We'll see just if Conflict Zone can break the prolonging habit when it blasts on to store shelves in the next few months."<p>
