			<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2">
			February&nbsp;12, 2001<p>
			<font size="1">DailyRadar was thoroughly impressed with the new flier. Here is some of what they had to say:<p>
"Not much can be made in the way of criticism; Iron Aces remains a solidly made title that may sputter at times, but certainly never explodes in flames. There's an instant replay feature of sorts that interrupts gameplay by showing off an enemy plane exploding when it's been struck by gunfire. Luckily, this feature can be turned off at will. The graphics are rather stolid and sometimes jaggy, but are certainly not intrusive or offensive in any way. The game simply and consistently provides competency in large doses, and emerges as the Dreamcast's best, most mindlessly fun plane shooter.<p>
<b>The Bottom Line:</b> We have a hit in our sights."<p>
